          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-06 04:49:16.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-21074 llite: send exec open flag to the MDS again",
        "message": "LU-21074 llite: send exec open flag to the MDS again\n\nSince the MDS open flag conversion, an exec through a cached dentry\nwould reach the MDS as a plain read open.  The conversion in\nll_kernel_to_mds_open_flags() maps __FMODE_EXEC to MDS_FMODE_EXECUTE,\nwhile the client open handle slots, mdc_intent_open_pack() and\nmds_pack_open_flags() test MDS_FMODE_EXEC or the kernel FMODE_EXEC.\nThe MDS then skipped mdt_write_deny(), so a file could be opened for\nwrite on one client while it was executing on another, and executed\nwhile open for write, and it checked MAY_READ instead of MAY_EXEC.\nExec opens through ll_atomic_open() still sent the exec flag, but were\nput in the read open handle slot.\n\nUse MDS_FMODE_EXEC for exec in every intent, whichever path built it,\nand test only that bit in mdc.  MDS_FMODE_EXECUTE is no longer used.\n\nDo not cache exec open handles, as LU-4398 does for write handles of\nexecutables.  A cached exec handle keeps the MDS denying write opens\nfrom other clients after the program has exited, until the open lock\nis cancelled.  Each exec now costs an open and a close RPC.\n\nAlso pass MDS_FMODE_* to ll_md_real_close() in ll_clear_inode(),\nwhose FMODE_EXEC would trip the assertion in ll_md_real_close() for a\ncached exec handle.\n\nWait in sanityn test_14ab-14c until the executable is running, and do\nnot overwrite the executable in test_14aa.  Add test_14ac to exec\nthrough a cached dentry in both directions, and to open for write\nafter the program has exited.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanityn\nFixes: 948fcacd8be4 (\"LU-12885 mds: add enums for MDS_OPEN flags (3/4)\")\nFixes: 19a2573e1633 (\"LU-12885 mds: add enums for MDS_OPEN flags (4/4)\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I5f074e29e074a08c154403ae765ad71c643ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
